"overview": "Colorado's Senate race is effectively settled. Incumbent Democrat John Hickenlooper sought and won a second term against Republican state senator Mark Baisley, with outlets including the Associated Press, the Denver Post, and Colorado Newsline calling the race on election day. Late polls from Keating Research, Research Co., and CU Boulder/YouGov all showed Hickenlooper ahead by roughly 18 to 22 points among likely voters.\n\nThe fundamentals favored the Democrat throughout: Colorado leans about six points Democratic, Hickenlooper raised more than $9.5 million to Baisley's roughly $140,000, and every major race rater rated the contest Solid or Safe Democratic. Prediction markets priced a Hickenlooper win at 99 percent. A self-funded independent, Bob Chew, spent over $3.5 million but did not alter the outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9917, "margin": 17.12}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9895, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9916, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.987, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9886, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9878, "margin": 16.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9912, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.994, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9898, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9915, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9938, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9899, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9876, "margin": 16.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.989, "margin": 17.2}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9887, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9898, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9905, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.989, "margin": 17.3}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9875, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.9898, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-1